Bamboo (Vietnamese Input Method) engine support for Fcitx

Based on https://github.com/BambooEngine/bamboo-core

Released under LGPLv2.1+

Requires:
Fcitx 5, go.

Install:
$ mkdir build && cd build
$ cmake -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=[prefix to fcitx5] ..
$ make
# make install

For typing without inline composition underlines or a preedit popup, enable
"Type directly into the application (Unicode)" in Bamboo's configuration.
This mode inserts each character immediately and replaces only the changed
suffix when you type accent keys. It requires the Unicode output charset.
Apps that support surrounding text use text replacement; other apps receive
Backspace events before the replacement text. Compatibility in the latter
case depends on the app processing forwarded keys in order and notifying the
input method when the cursor moves. Turn this option off to use composition
mode in an app that does not handle direct typing correctly.
Zen through GNOME's IBus bridge uses Backspace replacement when a web field
reports stale surrounding text. Its address bar retains normal text replacement.
Moving focus to another field resets this fallback.

For Telegram Desktop's Flatpak build, use its Fcitx Qt plugin with synchronous
key processing. Apply this application-specific override and restart Telegram:
$ flatpak override --user --env=QT_IM_MODULE=fcitx --env=QT_IM_MODULES=fcitx --env=FCITX_QT_USE_SYNC=1 org.telegram.desktop
For a native Qt build, launch it with the same environment variables.

To run the direct-input regression tests after building:
$ ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
